## Entry for the Table of Contents
This review summarizes the outer surface interaction of cucurbit[n]urils (OSIQ) in various simple Q[n]-based supramolecular frameworks (QSFs) and QSFs assembled via i) self-induced OSIQs; ii) anion-induced OSIQs; and iii) aromatic-induced OSIQs. The design and construction of QSFs via OSIQs with novel structures and specific functional properties can establish a new research direction in $\mathsf{Q}[\boldsymbol{n}]$ chemistry.
